    "result": "# PWA-C10 Auth submission boundaries: independent review\n\n**Verdict: SOURCE ACCEPT.** I found no MUST FIX.\n\nThis is based only on the source you pasted. Per your \"No tools/edits\" instruction I did not read the repo, write a plan file or call ExitPlanMode. The acceptance depends on Codex's mechanical inversion proving each of the 9 pages byte-identical to baseline `ea61500` except for the tag and import swaps.\n\n## Server Action serialization\n- **Imported actions:** `action={xAction}` passed from a Server Component page into the `'use client'` `OfflineForm` is a valid prop. Flight passes a server reference whose SSR form-action encoding is preserved, so the pre-hydration native POST keeps the original contract.\n- **Inline `'use server'` closures:** passing one as a prop to a client component is equally valid, and bound or captured arguments keep their encrypted encoding. \"Inline use-server preserved\" holds if the action expressions are untouched, which the inversion proves.\n- **Children:** the hidden inputs, labels, `<p>` hints and the child button are Server Component JSX passed as children. They serialize as RSC elements and `{...props}` forwards them unchanged.\n- **Hidden values:** `token_hash`, `intent_id`, `invitation_id` and `issuance` were already in both the HTML and the RSC payload of the original server-rendered `<form>`. Moving them under a client parent adds no new exposure. `value={undefined}` serializes as `$undefined` and renders the same way.\n- **Permissions and data:** no server data, permission check, gate or setup moves to the client. The pages stay Server Components and the wrapper receives only what the original form already emitted.\n\n## Form event ordering\n- **Order of handlers:** React 19 runs the `onSubmit` dispatch before its form-action submit listener. That listener returns early when `nativeEvent.defaultPrevented` is set.\n- **No pending state when blocked:** `refreshSignal` is a `useReducer` dispatch, not a transition. `didCurrentEventScheduleTransition()` is therefore false, so a blocked submit produces no host transition and no false pending state.\n- **Browser validation:** `required` and `minLength` checks run before the `submit` event fires. They behave as before.\n- **Disabled button while offline:** the disabled default button also stops implicit Enter submission. The `onSubmit` guard still covers the race where the device goes offline after the last render.\n- **Fields kept:** nothing is reset when a submit is blocked, so field values, including passwords, stay only in the current document's inputs. The wrapper never reads FormData or values, and stores, logs or queues nothing.\n\n## Pending status and props\n- `OfflineSubmitButton` renders inside the `<form>` that `OfflineForm` outputs. Its `useFormStatus` and the inner `SubmitButton`'s `useFormStatus` therefore read their own form's pending state, the same as the original child.\n- `label` and `pendingLabel` pass through unchanged. `disabled` and `ariaDescribedBy` are not set at any of the 13 sites, so the computed values are only the offline additions.\n- `className`, `action`, the attribute order differences between `className`/`action` sites and the bodies all pass through `{...props}`. The rendered DOM attributes are equivalent.\n\n## Overclaim and scope checks\n- **No JavaScript or not yet hydrated:** the server snapshot is `false`, so the SSR markup has no disabled button and no notice. The native POST path is the original one, so the \"no-JS behavior unchanged\" claim is accurate, not an overclaim.\n- **After dispatch:** a failure or unknown result after the request is sent behaves as before. The plan correctly makes no claim here, and the \"continuation\" notice text avoids implying anything about provider reachability.\n- **Sign-out and GET forms:** not in the 13 sites. They need to stay excluded, and the inversion check should assert they still use a plain `<form>`.\n\n## Non-blocking notes (no action needed)\n- `employee-account-activation/page.tsx` has two forms using the same `employee-password` IDs, but they render in separate branches. This is unchanged from baseline.\n- Each guarded form subscribes to its own online/offline listener, which is negligible.\n- **Unverified:** visual rendering is NOT VISUALLY VERIFIED, and real provider, session and role behavior plus R0–R8 remain OPEN. No phase closure follows from this review.",
